      "id": 1,
      "text": "Elsmere began in 1886 when developer Joshua Heald bought farmland and built the first suburb in northern Delaware.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elsmere%2C_Delaware",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Elsmere became an incorporated town in 1909, formalizing its municipal status for the first time.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elsmere%2C_Delaware",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1910 the Delaware State Fair Association built a fairgrounds in Elsmere that hosted horse, car, motorcycle races, vaudeville, and fireworks.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21,
        22,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elsmere%2C_Delaware",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Freight trains still pass through Elsmere along CSX’s Philadelphia Subdivision and East Penn’s Wilmington & Northern lines, interchanging at Elsmere Junction.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elsmere%2C_Delaware",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "A 336‑bed Veterans Administration hospital opened on Elsmere’s western edge in 1950, the ninth VA hospital built after World War II.",
